first reported and analyzed at https://github.com/helix-editor/helix/issues/5761. The issue contains some more context which is not relevant to the upstream report here. Bug has been reproduced with  VSCode and Helix.

Completions for missing macro arguments generate incorrect edits which replace incorrect tokens.
It's best explained with an example (this is actually a testcase from the PR to fix this):

# Reproduction Steps

* Open the file below with helix or vscode, `$0` and `$1` represents the cursor for the first and the second example respectively (they are not part of the document):

``` rust
macro_rules! foo {
    ($val:ident,  $val2: ident) => {
        $val $val2
    };
}

const BAR: u32 = 9;
fn main() {
    foo!(BAR, $0)
    foo!($1)
}
```



* Manually trigger completions (with `c-space` for vscode or `c-x` for ehlix) at either one of these points (**important: without typing any character**)
* Select and apply the `BAR` completion

# Expected Behavior

